# Credentials. Copy to .env and fill in what the machine actually needs.
#
# Assign nothing you do not have. An empty assignment is still an assignment:
# on the Pi the backend reads this file as well as /etc/describer/describer.env,
# and a bare "RDM_API_KEY=" here would blank the deployed key.

# Rail Data Marketplace API key, from the Live Arrival and Departure Boards
# (LDBWS) product. Never committed — .env is in .gitignore.
#RDM_API_KEY=

# Realtime Trains bearer token, used as the fallback source on the Pi. Request
# one from https://api-portal.rtt.io. It may be a long-life access token or a
# refresh token the client exchanges for short-life ones; either works.
#
# Leave this unset in development. The free tier is 1000 calls a day shared by
# every machine holding the token, so a dev session spends the live board's
# allowance. Set sources.fallback: null locally and work from the recorded
# fixtures in tests/fixtures/rtt_*.json instead.
#RTT_TOKEN=
